.Dd September 6, 2026
.Dt LOCALDEVICE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm localdevice
.Nd capability-plane device-node broker
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon is the capability system's provider for
.Dq Li system.Device .
It is a socket-free capability-plane service: it exposes the well-known name
.Dq Li system.Device
and serves each client on its own
.Xr mac_capability 4
channel.
On request it opens a named
.Pa /dev
leaf, narrows the resulting descriptor to exactly the rights the per-label
policy allows, and hands that descriptor back to the client over its channel.
.Pp
.Nm
sits just below
.Dq Li system.Filesystem :
.Xr tzfsd 8
brokers persistent storage, while
.Nm
brokers raw device nodes for the driver model.
.Pp
.Nm
is launched and supervised by
.Xr serviced 8
from the
.Pa /Capabilities/System/Device.cap
bundle; it is not started by
.Xr init 8 ,
and it is not intended to be run from the command line.
.Ss Born in capability mode
.Nm
never names a global path.
.Xr serviced 8
delivers
.Pa /dev
as an inherited directory descriptor
.Pq manifest Li directories = ["/dev"] ,
and
.Nm
opens each requested leaf beneath it with
.Xr openat 2 .
It enters capability mode before serving any client and forks a
.Xr pdfork 2 Ns 'd
worker per connection.
.Ss Open protocol
A client sends an OPEN request naming a single
.Pa /dev
leaf and a wanted-rights mask
.Pq Dv DEVICECMP_RIGHT_READ , WRITE , IOCTL , MMAP , SEEK , EVENT .
.Nm
rejects any name that is empty, contains a
.Ql / ,
begins with a
.Ql \&. ,
or is
.Ql \&.\&. :
the name must be a single leaf component.
The delivered descriptor is capped with
.Xr cap_rights_limit 2
to the granted rights
.Pq always including Dv CAP_FSTAT ,
optionally further restricted to a per-device
.Xr cap_ioctls_limit 2
command whitelist, and hardened so it can be transferred exactly once
.Pq this delivery
and no further.
.Ss Policy
Access is
.Em default-deny .
The compiled-in policy grants nothing; an optional
.Pa device.conf
file in the unit's
.Pa Config/
directory grants, per client label, one
.Pa /dev
leaf a set of rights.
A request whose
.Pq label , device
pair matches no entry is refused with
.Er EACCES ;
the granted rights are the intersection of the wanted mask and the entry's
maximum.
.Ss List protocol
A client sends a LIST request to enumerate the devices its own label is
permitted to open.
The enumeration is strictly scoped to the connecting channel's unforgeable
label, never a wire argument, so a caller can only ever see its own entries; a
label with no policy entry lists empty, preserving
.Em default-deny .
Each returned entry names one
.Pa /dev
leaf, the rights that label may be granted for it, and a flag set when the
entry carries a per-device ioctl whitelist.
The request carries a
.Va cursor
and the reply a
.Va next_cursor ,
so a policy larger than one reply is paged; the additive request fields must be
zero.
The reply mints no descriptor.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /Capabilities/System/Device.cap" -compact
.It Pa /dev
device directory delivered as an inherited descriptor
.It Pa /Capabilities/System/Device.cap
capability bundle shipping
.Nm
.It Pa /Capabilities/System/Device.cap/Units/localdevice.unit/Config/device.conf
per-label device policy
.El
.Sh DTRACE PROBES
The
.Dq localdevice
provider exports
.Sy open ,
which fires when an OPEN is resolved with the client label, the requested
.Pa /dev
leaf, the rights actually granted
.Pq the request intersected with policy, zero on denial ,
and the errno, and
.Sy list ,
which fires when a LIST page is produced with the client label, the requested
cursor, the number of entries filled, and the errno.
The errno argument is zero on success.
Device contents are never probe arguments.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
.Xr cap_ioctls_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_rights_limit 2 ,
.Xr openat 2 ,
.Xr pdfork 2 ,
.Xr mac_capability 4 ,
.Xr serviced 8 ,
.Xr tzfsd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
daemon appeared in
.Fx 5BSD
as the capability-plane device-node broker.
